    "narrative": "The core of our lineup today is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts the day\u2019s highest efficiency score of 76.16. He is a must-start against Paddack, whose 4.52 xERA offers a prime environment for **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** to capitalize on high-leverage opportunities in the two-hole. Close behind is **Geraldo Perdomo** (72.67), who benefits from an exceptional park factor (+14%) and favorable SP skill metrics (+18%) against Sugano. While **Geraldo Perdomo** typically flies under the radar, his position in the three-hole combined with these environmental variables makes him a superior play over more traditional power hitters today. Similarly, **Luis Arraez** (66.78) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65) leverage the high park factor at their venue to push past several higher-base-projection counterparts, providing a high-floor offensive foundation.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the day involved **Bryson Stott** (54.06), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While his platoon advantage against Chandler is enticing (+13%), he is docked by a combination of a poor park factor and a low spot in the batting order, which suppresses his run-scoring potential compared to the high-volume opportunities afforded to **Daulton Varsho** and **Taylor Ward**. We are closely monitoring the risk profile of **Lawrence Butler** (52.64); he faces the toughest matchup of our starters against McDonald, whose 2.87 xERA acts as a significant drag on our scoring ceiling. If the weather conditions shift or lineup changes pull him from the seven-hole, we will be forced to reconsider his position in the utility slot to preserve our games-played efficiency. **Gavin Sheets** was excluded entirely today, as his sub-40 score against a formidable opponent like Gilbert confirms he belongs on the bench to preserve cap space for more advantageous matchups later this week.",
